PREAMBLE
==============================================================================

Plumlang is a programming language, compiler, virtual machine, standard
library, and set of tools (together, "the Software"). We publish its source
code openly so that anyone can read it, learn from it, try it, and help make
it better.

We also want Plumlang to be a sustainable project. Building and maintaining a
language that runs everywhere takes years of work, and that work is funded
by the businesses that rely on it. This license therefore draws one simple
line:

  * If you are learning, teaching, experimenting, evaluating, or building
    something for yourself that you do not sell or use to run a business,
    Plumlang is free for you.

  * If you use Plumlang to make money, to run a business, or to ship it to
    other people as part of a product or service, you need a commercial
    license from us.

Programs you write in the Plumlang language are yours. This license governs
the Software itself, not the code you write with it. The full terms below
are binding. This preamble only explains their purpose; it is not part of
the terms.

